window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-8d926b82884d5f99"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"codex-security-cicd-overview\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"cicd-codex-security\">在 CI/CD 中使用 Codex Security</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>在 CI 中运行 Codex Security，可检查拉取请求或合并请求中的变更、扫描默认分支，并保留发现项和覆盖信息。有关工作流、报告处理和策略执行方式，请参阅对应 CI 提供商的指南。</p> <p><a id=\"prepare-the-workflow\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">准备工作流</h2> <p>运行扫描需要拥有 Codex Security 访问权限。在 CI 提供商的密钥存储区中，将 OpenAI API 密钥保存为 <code>CODEX_SECURITY_API_KEY</code>，然后将其映射到扫描进程的 <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code> 环境变量。</p> <p>只扫描你信任的代码仓库和变更。扫描会使用运行器的本地权限，且不会暂停等待审批。请将无关凭据和部署步骤放在单独的作业中。</p> <p><a id=\"use-an-approved-daybreak-model\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"daybreak\">使用已批准的 Daybreak 模型</h3> <p>如要通过<a href=\"#/article/a-04f6dcc4a4fe6044?anchor=trusted-access-for-cyber\">网络安全可信访问计划（Trusted Access for Cyber）</a>使用 Daybreak Blue，请将 GitHub Action 的 <code>model</code> 输入设为 <code>gpt-6-sol</code>，并将 <code>cyber-access-program</code> 设为 <code>daybreak_blue</code>。直接通过 CLI 扫描时，请使用 <code>--model gpt-6-sol</code> 和 <code>--cyber-access-program daybreak_blue</code>。</p> <p>API 密钥所属的项目必须已启用 Daybreak Blue，并且有权使用所选模型。设置模型或计划名称并不会授予访问权限。Action 的具体设置请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-cb94fa07f6e7450c?anchor=configure-optional-daybreak-access\">配置可选的 Daybreak 访问权限</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-an-integration\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">选择集成方式</h2> <p><a id=\"add-the-github-actions-workflow\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"github-actions\">添加 GitHub Actions 工作流</h3> <p>如要检查拉取请求或定期扫描代码仓库，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-cb94fa07f6e7450c\">GitHub Actions 指南</a>。Codex Security Action 会安装 CLI、保存报告，并生成作业摘要和源代码注释。该指南包含运行器设置、可选的 Daybreak 访问权限、SARIF 上传和严重级别策略执行说明。</p> <p><a id=\"add-the-gitlab-cicd-pipeline\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"gitlab-cicd\">添加 GitLab CI/CD 流水线</h3> <p>如要扫描合并请求、默认分支或安排定期扫描，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-0c31a6fce966b88c\">GitLab CI/CD 指南</a>。可以先运行只扫描、不阻止合并的流水线，再逐步采用报告处理、策略执行和可选的已验证修复流程。</p> <p><a id=\"use-another-ci-system\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"ci\">使用其他 CI 系统</h3> <p>安装公开发布的 <code>@openai/codex-security</code> 软件包，然后直接运行 CLI。使用 <code>--auth api-key</code> 指定 API 密钥身份验证，选择全仓库扫描或差异扫描，并将输出保存到 Git 工作树之外的私有目录。运行器必须提供 <a href=\"#/article/a-1716f9f1a07bca7e?anchor=check-the-prerequisites\">CLI 快速入门</a>中说明的依赖项。</p> <p>扫描选项、差异修订版本、报告格式、状态与输出目录，以及重试行为，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34\">CLI 参考</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-a-severity-policy\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">选择严重级别策略</h2> <p>先从建议性结果开始。在决定哪些情况应阻止合并之前，先检查有代表性的发现项、扫描覆盖范围、费用和运行时间。</p> <p>评估时既要看发现项，也要看扫描是否完整。严重级别策略会检查本次扫描中达到或超过配置阈值的发现项；代码仓库摘要中此前尚未关闭的发现项不会影响该策略。扫描不完整时，即使没有报告发现项，也可能仍有部分区域未被检查。</p> <p>在 Action <code>action-v0.3.0</code> 版本中，“扫描已完成”表示所配置的分析已生成有效结果。范围排除项、延期调查和其他覆盖说明不会绕过严重级别策略。扫描器错误和必要报告错误都会导致作业失败。CLI <code>0.3.0</code> 在输入、执行、结果完整性或必要输出发生故障时返回退出代码 <code>2</code>。评估扫描结果时请检查 <code>coverage.json</code>；扫描完成并不代表已经发现所有漏洞。</p> <p>如使用 GitHub Actions，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-cb94fa07f6e7450c?anchor=choose-a-severity-policy\">选择严重级别策略</a>；如使用 GitLab，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-0c31a6fce966b88c?anchor=separate-reporting-from-policy-enforcement\">将报告与策略执行分开</a>。直接集成 CLI 时，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=exit-codes-and-signals\">严重级别策略与退出代码</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"codex-security-cicd-overview\">Codex Security CI/CD overview</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Run Codex Security in CI to review pull-request or merge-request changes, scan your default branch, and preserve findings and coverage. See your CI provider's guide for the workflow, report handling, and enforcement options.</p> <h2 id=\"prepare-the-workflow\">Prepare the workflow</h2> <p>Running scans requires Codex Security access. Store an OpenAI API key in your CI provider's secret store as <code>CODEX_SECURITY_API_KEY</code>, then map it to the scan process's <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code> environment variable.</p> <p>Run scans only for repositories and changes you trust. Scans use the runner's local permissions and don't pause for approval. Keep unrelated credentials and deployment steps in separate jobs.</p> <h3 id=\"use-an-approved-daybreak-model\">Use an approved Daybreak model</h3> <p>For Daybreak Blue access through <a href=\"#/article/a-04f6dcc4a4fe6044?anchor=trusted-access-for-cyber\">Trusted Access for Cyber</a>, set the GitHub Action's <code>model</code> input to <code>gpt-6-sol</code> and <code>cyber-access-program</code> to <code>daybreak_blue</code>. For direct CLI scans, use <code>--model gpt-6-sol</code> and <code>--cyber-access-program daybreak_blue</code>.</p> <p>Use an API key from a project that has Daybreak Blue enabled and access to the selected model. Setting the model or program does not grant access. See <a href=\"#/article/a-cb94fa07f6e7450c?anchor=configure-optional-daybreak-access\">Configure optional Daybreak access</a> for the Action settings.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-an-integration\">Choose an integration</h2> <h3 id=\"add-the-github-actions-workflow\">Add the GitHub Actions workflow</h3> <p>Use the <a href=\"#/article/a-cb94fa07f6e7450c\">GitHub Actions guide</a> for pull-request checks and scheduled repository scans. The Codex Security Action installs the CLI, saves reports, and adds a job summary and source annotations. The guide includes runner setup, optional Daybreak access, SARIF upload, and severity enforcement.</p> <h3 id=\"add-the-gitlab-cicd-pipeline\">Add the GitLab CI/CD pipeline</h3> <p>Use the <a href=\"#/article/a-0c31a6fce966b88c\">GitLab CI/CD guide</a> for merge-request, default-branch, and scheduled scans. Start with a scan-only pipeline, then adopt report handling, policy enforcement, and optional verified remediation.</p> <h3 id=\"use-another-ci-system\">Use another CI system</h3> <p>Install the public <code>@openai/codex-security</code> package and run the CLI directly. Use <code>--auth api-key</code>, choose a repository or diff scan, and save the output in a private directory outside the Git worktree. Your runner must provide the dependencies described in the <a href=\"#/article/a-1716f9f1a07bca7e?anchor=check-the-prerequisites\">CLI quickstart</a>.</p> <p>See the <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34\">CLI reference</a> for scan options, diff revisions, report formats, state and output directories, and retry behavior.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-a-severity-policy\">Choose a severity policy</h2> <p>Start with advisory results. Review representative findings, scan coverage, cost, and runtime before deciding which outcomes should block a merge.</p> <p>Evaluate both findings and scan completeness. The severity policy evaluates findings from the current scan at or above the configured threshold. Earlier open findings in the repository summary don't affect that policy. An incomplete scan can leave areas without a review even when it reports no findings.</p> <p>In the Action release <code>action-v0.3.0</code>, a completed scan means the configured analysis produced a valid result. Scope exclusions, deferred investigations, and other coverage notes do not bypass the severity policy. Scanner and required reporting errors fail the job. CLI <code>0.3.0</code> returns exit code <code>2</code> for input, execution, result-integrity, or required-output failures. Review <code>coverage.json</code> when assessing the result; completion does not certify that every vulnerability was found.</p> <p>Configure enforcement in the <a href=\"#/article/a-cb94fa07f6e7450c?anchor=choose-a-severity-policy\">GitHub Actions guide</a> or the <a href=\"#/article/a-0c31a6fce966b88c?anchor=separate-reporting-from-policy-enforcement\">GitLab CI/CD guide</a>. For direct CLI integrations, see <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=exit-codes-and-signals\">severity enforcement and exit codes</a>.</p>"};
